      "nets": ["TSC_G2_IO2"],
      "observed": "Net TSC_G2_IO2 contains U2 pin 57 (PB5), R8 pin 1, and all GND nodes (e.g., U2 VSS pins, J1 pin 5). A2 pin 1 (BTN) is on a separate net Net-(A2-BTN) with R8 pin 2.",
      "expected": "TSC_G2_IO2 should connect U2 pin 57 (PB5) through R8 to A2 pin 1 (BTN), and should not be connected to GND. A2 pin 2 (SHLD) should be the only A2 pin tied to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"21\") (name \"TSC_G2_IO2\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"57\") (pinfunction \"PB5\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) ... (node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) ...)"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"10\") (name \"Net-(A2-BTN)\") ... (node (ref \"A2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"BTN\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "TSC_G2_IO2: U2 pin 57 (PB5) — R8 (1 kΩ series resistor) — A2 pin \"BTN\" (the touch electrode)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "A2 pin \"SHLD\" (shield) ties to GND"}
      ],
      "impact": "PB5 is shorted to ground, and the touch electrode is connected to ground through R8 instead of to PB5. The capacitive touch button will not function, and PB5 is held low.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a short-to-ground anomaly on the capacitive touch net: TSC_G2_IO2 is merged with GND, grounding U2 pin 57 (PB5) and R8 pin 1, while the touch electrode A2 pin 1 is isolated on a separate net. This breaks the intended TSC connection described in the specification."
}

